#. module: account_ebics
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_account_ebics
msgid ""
"======================\n"
"EBICS Banking Protocol\n"
"======================\n"
"\n"
"**Exchange files directly with your banks from Odoo, with no portal and "
"nobody logging in.**\n"
"\n"
"EBICS, the Electronic Banking Internet Communication Standard, is the "
"channel European\n"
"banks open to companies that want their software to talk to the bank. Bank "
"statements are\n"
"downloaded on a schedule and payment files are uploaded from Odoo, "
"authenticated by your\n"
"own cryptographic keys instead of a login page.\n"
"\n"
"This module implements that protocol in Odoo. It is developed and maintained "
"by\n"
"Noviat, and follows each new version of Odoo, which matters when a bank "
"connection has to\n"
"survive your next migration.\n"
"\n"
"If you are still working out whether EBICS is the right channel for you, we "
"explain it\n"
"without the jargon, with screen recordings of the flow in Odoo, on\n"
"`noviat.com/ebics <https://www.noviat.com/ebics>`_.\n"
"\n"
".. image:: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Noviat/account_ebics/19.0/"
"account_ebics/static/description/ebics_flow.png\n"
"   :alt: Statements come down as camt.053 or camt.052 files, payment files "
"go up as pain.001 or pain.008, and your keys stay on your own server\n"
"   :width: 100%\n"
"\n"
"What you get\n"
"============\n"
"\n"
"- **Statements that arrive on their own.** A scheduled task collects the "
"files your bank\n"
"  publishes, for every account, and processes them into bank statements.\n"
"- **Payments that leave the same way.** A payment batch or a payment order "
"is uploaded to\n"
"  the bank in the format the bank expects, without exporting a file and re-"
"uploading it\n"
"  somewhere else.\n"
"- **Several companies, one connection.** Keys are held per bank rather than "
"per company:\n"
"  when fifteen entities bank with the same institution, the bank sends a "
"single daily file\n"
"  carrying fifteen statements and the module puts each statement in the "
"right company.\n"
"- **No bank credentials in Odoo.** The connection uses your own company "
"keys, generated on\n"
"  your side and kept on your server. Access to the EBICS configuration is a "
"permission of\n"
"  its own ('EBICS Manager'), separate from ordinary accounting rights.\n"
"- **A test mode, where your bank offers one.** French banks accept a test "
"flag, so a file\n"
"  can be submitted and validated before anything is switched to production. "
"German and\n"
"  Swiss banks generally do not: there the first payment is a real one, kept "
"small and sent\n"
"  to an account you control.\n"
"- **A trace of every exchange.** Each download and each upload is a record, "
"with the file\n"
"  it carried, the moment it happened and the user behind it.\n"
"\n"
"**EBICS 2.4**, **EBICS 2.5** and **EBICS 3.0** are supported. EBICS 3.0, the "
"current\n"
"specification since December 2022, names what is exchanged with BTF instead "
"of the\n"
"country-specific order type codes of EBICS 2.x. Many banks still run 2.4 or "
"2.5 in parallel.\n"
"\n"
"What travels over the link\n"
"==========================\n"
"\n"
"- **Coming in:** camt.053 for the end of day statement, camt.052 for "
"intraday movements\n"
"  where the bank offers them, and national formats such as the French "
"CFONB.\n"
"- **Going out:** pain.001 for credit transfers and pain.008 for direct "
"debits, generated by\n"
"  Odoo from your payment batches.\n"
"\n"
"We do not process MT940 statements: the format carries bank and country "
"specific variations,\n"
"and the Odoo community stopped maintaining a general parser for it after "
"Odoo 10. Where a\n"
"bank publishes camt.053 alongside it, which is now the usual case, that is "
"the format to use.\n"
"\n"
"Which banks\n"
"===========\n"
"\n"
"Any bank that publishes an EBICS access point can be connected. The standard "
"is maintained by\n"
"EBICS SC, a company held by the German, French, Swiss and Austrian banking "
"bodies\n"
"(DK, CFONB, SIX and PSA), and it is the standard corporate channel in those "
"countries.\n"
"\n"
"To check a specific bank before you start, joonis publishes a public "
"directory at\n"
"`joonis.de/en/fintech/banks <https://www.joonis.de/en/fintech/banks/>`_. "
"Enter a BIC and it\n"
"returns the SEPA services the bank offers, the EBICS versions it supports "
"and its Host-ID.\n"
"\n"
"A bank missing from that directory is not a no: it is joonis' own list, not "
"an official\n"
"register. Ask your bank whether it publishes an EBICS access point.\n"
"\n"
"What it costs\n"
"=============\n"
"\n"
"**This module is free software**, published under LGPL-3. There is no "
"licence fee, no\n"
"subscription and no per-connection charge from Noviat.\n"
"\n"
"It does however rely on the `fintech <https://pypi.python.org/pypi/"
"fintech>`_ library from\n"
"joonis, and that library requires a **commercial licence for production "
"use**: as soon as\n"
"you upload SEPA files with more than five transactions, retrieve statements "
"older than the\n"
"last three days, or use the distributed signature. The licence is contracted "
"directly with\n"
"joonis, not with Noviat.\n"
"\n"
"joonis charges a one-off setup fee plus a monthly fee per EBICS user id. "
"Current pricing is\n"
"published on\n"
"`joonis.de <https://www.joonis.de/en/fintech/prices/>`_.\n"
"\n"
"Your bank may also charge a subscription for the EBICS channel itself. It "
"varies from one\n"
"bank to another and is billed by the bank, separately from anything on the "
"Odoo side.\n"
"\n"
"Requirements\n"
"============\n"
"\n"
"The module depends on two Python libraries:\n"
"\n"
"- `fintech <https://pypi.python.org/pypi/fintech>`_\n"
"- `cryptography <https://pypi.python.org/pypi/cryptography>`_\n"
"\n"
"Because the connection needs a Python library and your key files on the "
"server, it runs on\n"
"**Odoo.sh** or on an **on-premise** installation.\n"
"\n"
"The EBICS test mode for uploads requires fintech 4.3.4 or higher for EBICS 2."
"x and fintech\n"
"7.2.7 or higher for EBICS 3.0. SWIFT 3SKey support requires fintech 6.4 or "
"higher, and the signature passphrase\n"
"fintech 7.3.1 or higher.\n"
"\n"
"Fintech licence\n"
"---------------\n"
"\n"
"With a fintech licence, add its parameters to the ``[options]`` section of "
"the Odoo server\n"
"configuration file:\n"
"\n"
"- ``fintech_register_name``: the name of the licensee;\n"
"- ``fintech_register_keycode``: the keycode of the licensed version.\n"
"\n"
"Example::\n"
"\n"
" ; fintech\n"
" fintech_register_name = MyCompany\n"
" fintech_register_keycode = AB1CD-E2FG-3H-IJ4K-5L\n"
"\n"
"Companion modules\n"
"=================\n"
"\n"
"From this repository:\n"
"\n"
"- **EBICS - Odoo Enterprise Integration** (``account_ebics_oe``): required "
"on Odoo\n"
"  Enterprise; installed automatically.\n"
"- **EBICS - Batch Payments (Odoo Enterprise)** "
"(``account_ebics_batch_payment``): uploads\n"
"  the batch payments of the Odoo Enterprise ``account_batch_payment`` "
"module.\n"
"- **EBICS - Payment Orders (OCA)** (``account_ebics_payment_order``): "
"uploads the payment\n"
"  orders of the OCA ``account_payment_order`` module\n"
"  (`OCA/bank-payment <https://github.com/OCA/bank-payment>`_).\n"
"\n"
"To process the downloaded statements, install the module of each format you "
"receive:\n"
"\n"
"- **camt.053, camt.052 and camt.054**: ``account_statement_import_camt``\n"
"  (`OCA/bank-statement-import <https://github.com/OCA/bank-statement-"
"import>`_). For\n"
"  camt.053, the Odoo Enterprise ``account_bank_statement_import_camt`` works "
"too.\n"
"- **French CFONB**: ``account_statement_import_fr_cfonb``\n"
"  (`OCA/l10n-france <https://github.com/OCA/l10n-france>`_).\n"
"\n"
"Recommended with several financial journals: ``account_usability``\n"
"(`OCA/account-financial-tools <https://github.com/OCA/account-financial-"
"tools>`_), which adds\n"
"accounting menus such as a list of all bank statements, including those "
"downloaded by the\n"
"scheduled import.\n"
"\n"
"Getting your bank online\n"
"========================\n"
"\n"
"The configuration on the Odoo side takes fifteen to thirty minutes. What "
"sets the pace of a\n"
"project is the bank, and it is almost never for a technical reason:\n"
"\n"
"- **The bank opens the access.** You receive the host ID, the address of the "
"access point,\n"
"  your partner and user identifiers, and a letter carrying the hash values "
"of the bank's keys.\n"
"- **INI and HIA.** Odoo generates your key pairs for signature, "
"authentication and encryption,\n"
"  sends the public keys to the bank and produces the initialisation letters, "
"which you print,\n"
"  sign and send. The bank compares them by hand with the keys it received "
"online.\n"
"- **HPB.** Once the bank has activated your access, you retrieve its public "
"keys and compare\n"
"  their hash values with the letter it sent you. That comparison is what "
"makes the channel\n"
"  trustworthy.\n"
"- **The first exchange.** Statements come down first. Payments follow, as a "
"test file where\n"
"  the bank supports the test flag, otherwise as a real transfer of a small "
"amount.\n"
"\n"
"Count in weeks per bank rather than days, and start the contract and the "
"paperwork early.\n"
"\n"
"Installation\n"
"============\n"
"\n"
"**Upgrading from versions prior to account_ebics 20.0.1.1.0**:\n"
"If ``account_ebics_batch`` is present in your addons path, remove its "
"directory\n"
"before running the upgrade. Its functionality has been merged into this "
"module.\n"
"\n"
"If the directory is left on disk, the upgrade completes correctly but Odoo "
"will\n"
"rediscover ``account_ebics_batch`` on the next restart and add it back to "
"the\n"
"module list as *Not Installed*. It will not cause errors, but removing it "
"keeps\n"
"the installation clean.\n"
"\n"
"Configuration\n"
"=============\n"
"\n"
"The menus are those of Odoo Enterprise; on Odoo Community, the application "
"is called\n"
"*Invoicing* instead of *Accounting*.\n"
"\n"
"**Who may configure.** In *Settings > Users*, add the users who maintain the "
"EBICS\n"
"configuration to the **EBICS Manager** group.\n"
"\n"
"**File formats.** In *Accounting > Configuration > EBICS > EBICS File "
"Formats*, check that the\n"
"formats you exchange with your banks are defined; the common ones are "
"created at\n"
"installation. A missing format can be reported on\n"
"`GitHub <https://github.com/Noviat/account_ebics/issues>`_.\n"
"\n"
"A download format can carry a **Download Process Method**, run by the "
"*Process* button of a\n"
"downloaded file: ``camt.053``, ``camt.052``, ``camt.054`` and ``cfonb120``. "
"Each needs the\n"
"module of its format (see Companion modules); Odoo tells you which one when "
"it is missing.\n"
"\n"
"**Bank connections.** In *Accounting > Configuration > EBICS > EBICS "
"Configuration*, create one\n"
"connection per bank contract, with the identifiers your bank sent you.\n"
"\n"
".. image:: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Noviat/account_ebics/19.0/"
"account_ebics/static/description/ebics_download.png\n"
"   :alt: A downloaded camt.053 statement file in Odoo, before processing\n"
"   :width: 100%\n"
"\n"
"Scheduled import\n"
"----------------\n"
"\n"
"A scheduled action **EBICS Batch Import** is created **inactive** at "
"installation, with a\n"
"daily interval. Activate it in *Settings > Technical > Automation > "
"Scheduled Actions*\n"
"(developer mode), and adapt its interval if needed.\n"
"\n"
"The action runs the following method on all confirmed connections::\n"
"\n"
"  model._batch_import()\n"
"\n"
"To limit it to specific connections, pass their ids::\n"
"\n"
"  model._batch_import(ebics_config_ids=[1, 3])\n"
"\n"
"Batch Import Logs are listed under *EBICS Processing > Batch Import Logs*.\n"
"\n"
"Usage\n"
"=====\n"
"\n"
"The **EBICS Processing** menu, in the top bar of the Accounting application, "
"lists the\n"
"downloaded and uploaded files and offers manual downloads and uploads.\n"
"\n"
"Downloaded files are processed into bank statements. Uploads are launched "
"from the payment\n"
"batch or the payment order, with the format set in the configuration: on the "
"payment\n"
"mode for a payment order, on the journal's payment method for a batch "
"payment.\n"
"\n"
"Every run of the automatic download via the **EBICS Batch Import** scheduled "
"action\n"
"creates a **Batch Import Log** that records which files were processed and "
"what went wrong;\n"
"the *Reprocess* button retries any files still in draft until all errors are "
"cleared.\n"
"\n"
".. image:: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Noviat/account_ebics/19.0/"
"account_ebics/static/description/ebics_upload.png\n"
"   :alt: Uploading a pain.001 SEPA credit transfer file over EBICS 3.0, with "
"the test mode option\n"
"   :width: 100%\n"
"\n"
"Diagnostics\n"
"===========\n"
"\n"
"To diagnose the connection with your bank, add this line to the Odoo server "
"configuration\n"
"file::\n"
"\n"
" log_handler = fintech.ebics:DEBUG\n"
"\n"
"EBICS return codes\n"
"------------------\n"
"\n"
"During an upload or a download, your bank may return an error code, for "
"example::\n"
"\n"
" EBICS Functional Error:\n"
" EBICS_NO_DOWNLOAD_DATA_AVAILABLE (code: 90005)\n"
"\n"
"The codes are explained on `ebics.org <https://www.ebics.org>`_ and in the "
"``doc`` folder of\n"
"this module (``EBICS_Annex1_ReturnCodes``).\n"
"\n"
"EBICS TS (Transport and Signature) and EBICS EDS (Electronic Distributed "
"Signature)\n"
"-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n"
"\n"
"When configuring the bank connection as EBICS T, Odoo prepares the file and "
"holds no signing\n"
"credentials at all: the payment is approved in your own signing application, "
"which is what\n"
"a segregation of duties policy usually demands.\n"
"If you prefer not to do this or when the bank's web/mobile banking app does "
"not support\n"
"unsigned payment files, you can upload signed files.\n"
"In this case, the signing key sits on your Odoo server, and you can protect "
"it with\n"
"a separate signature passphrase that is never stored and is asked for every "
"signed transaction.\n"
"\n"
"You can also explore the use of external signing apps such as BankingVEU\n"
"(`Android <https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=subsembly."
"bankingveu>`_,\n"
"`iOS <https://apps.apple.com/de/app/bankingveu/id1578694190>`_).\n"
"\n"
"Roadmap\n"
"=======\n"
"\n"
"- Import externally generated keys and certificates (today only the 3SKey "
"signature\n"
"  certificate).\n"
"- Support the SWIFT 3SKey signing JavaScript library\n"
"  (`SConnect <https://www2.swift.com/3skey/help/sconnect.html>`_).\n"
"\n"
"Issues and pull requests are welcome on\n"
"`GitHub <https://github.com/Noviat/account_ebics>`_.\n"
"\n"
"Changelog\n"
"=========\n"
"\n"
"20.0.1.1.0 (2026-11-17)\n"
"------------------------\n"
"\n"
"The automated download of EBICS files (bank statements, payment status "
"reports) was up to\n"
"Odoo 19.0 provided by the ``account_ebics_batch`` module.\n"
"This functionality has now been integrated into the base ``account_ebics`` "
"module.\n"
"\n"
"Credits\n"
"=======\n"
"\n"
"This module is developed and maintained by `Noviat <https://www.noviat."
"com>`_, Odoo\n"
"integrator in Belgium, specialised in accounting and finance since 2009.\n"
"\n"
"We implement it, we configure the connection with your banks and we support "
"you through the\n"
"first cycles. If you want help getting a bank online, tell us which banks "
"you use:\n"
"https://www.noviat.com/ebics\n"
msgstr ""

